# Update docs with every commit

When committing (or preparing a commit), update project docs in the same change if the work affects them. Do not ship a commit that leaves docs stale.

## Where docs live

- `README.md` — play instructions, scripts, design index, status
- `docs/PLAN.md` — stack, architecture, simulation, phases, non-goals
- `docs/controls.md` — physics and juice knobs
- `docs/ios.md` — iOS device / simulator runbook
- `docs/adr/` — architecture decisions (add a new ADR only for durable choices)

## When to update

Update the matching file(s) in the same commit:

- New or changed npm scripts, play/build/deploy flow → `README.md`
- Stack, architecture, phases, or non-goals → `docs/PLAN.md`
- Config knobs, feel, FX timings → `docs/controls.md`
- Signing, Capacitor, Xcode, device run steps → `docs/ios.md`
- A lasting technical choice (keep vs rewrite) → new or updated ADR
- Status that is no longer true (e.g. "not on device yet") → `README.md` Status

Skip docs only when the change is purely internal and nothing a player, builder, or future agent would read has changed (typos in comments, test-only refactors with the same behavior).

## How

- Edit docs in the same commit as the code, not a follow-up.
- Prefer small factual edits over rewriting the whole file.
- Do not invent features in docs that the commit does not include.
